e (deferDelete, cancelPendingDelete, the timeout callback) touches both in the same breath, but it's the kind of duplicate-source-of-truth that the crash above grew out of \u2014 a single `Map<id, timerHandle>` in a ref, with `pendingDeleteIds` derived from `Array.from(map.keys())` (or driving toast render off the map directly), would remove one of the two places a future edit has to remember to update.", "verdict": "CONFIRMED"}]}, "session_id": "56a4d996-1bdf-4be3-85b0-80157f9d2990"}}
