{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:05:38Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 135, "kind": "message", "text": "## Review summary\n\n**Will block**\n\n- **`frontend/src/App.jsx:125` (Alan Heitkotter \u2014 failure paths) / `frontend/src/components/UndoToast.jsx:6`** \u2014 `pendingDeleteIds` is never reconciled against `tasks`, so when a pending-delete task disappears from `tasks` via some *other* refresh, the toast crashes. Concrete repro: delete a completed task (leaves it pending-undo, still in `tasks`), then click \"Clear completed\" before the 5s window elapses. That bulk-deletes the (done) task server-side and refreshes `tasks`, which no longer contains it \u2014 but `pendingDeleteIds` still does. `tasks.find(...)` returns `undefined`, and `UndoToast.jsx:6`'s `key={task.id}` throws on it. No error boundary exists, so this is a full UI crash, not a cosmetic glitch. This is exactly the race the spec's own AC6 anticipates (Clear Completed vs. a pending delete) \u2014 the code handles the async 404 from that race but not this synchronous state-desync from it.\n\n**Will comment**\n\n- **`frontend/src/App.jsx:19` (Christopher Zipp \u2014 reuse/data modelling)** \u2014 `pendingDeleteIds` (state) and `pendingDeleteTimers.current` (ref Map) track the identical key set in two places, always mutated together. Not a bug today, but it's the kind of duplicate source of truth that produced the blocker above; collapsing to one `Map<id, timerHandle>` (deriving the id list from its keys) removes a spot a future edit has to remember to touch twice.\n\n**Worth considering**\n\n- None.\n\nEverything else checks out: the frontend-only design decision is sound and well-justified, all six acceptance criteria are otherwise met (immediate hide, exact-state restore since nothing is mutated, 5s auto-delete, done-state preserved, independent multi-undo via array+Map, 404 swallowed on the *timer* path), `TaskList.jsx`/`api.js`/backend correctly left untouched, and the CSS/a11y choices match the design doc and existing `.error`/`TaskCounts` conventions.\n\nVERDICT: changes-requested", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "56a4d996-1bdf-4be3-85b0-80157f9d2990"}}
{"ts": "2026-08-17T13:05:38Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 136, "kind": "status", "text": "## Review summary\n\n**Will block**\n\n- **`frontend/src/App.jsx:125` (Alan Heitkotter \u2014 failure paths) / `frontend/src/components/UndoToast.jsx:6`** \u2014 `pendingDeleteIds` is never reconciled against `tasks`, so when a pending-delete task disappears from `tasks` via some *other* refresh, the toast crashes. Concrete repro: delete a completed task (leaves it pending-undo, still in `tasks`), then click \"Clear completed\" before the 5s window elapses. That bulk-deletes the (done) task server-side and refreshes `tasks`, which no longer contains it \u2014 but `pendingDeleteIds` still does. `tasks.find(...)` returns `undefined`, and `UndoToast.jsx:6`'s `key={task.id}` throws on it. No error boundary exists, so this is a full UI crash, not a cosmetic glitch. This is exactly the race the spec's own AC6 anticipates (Clear Completed vs. a pending delete) \u2014 the code handles the async 404 from that race but not this synchronous state-desync from it.\n\n**Will comment**\n\n- **`frontend/src/App.jsx:19` (Christopher Zipp \u2014 reuse/data modelling)** \u2014 `pendingDeleteIds` (state) and `pendingDeleteTimers.current` (ref Map) track the identical key set in two places, always mutated together. Not a bug today, but it's the kind of duplicate source of truth that produced the blocker above; collapsing to one `Map<id, timerHandle>` (deriving the id list from its keys) removes a spot a future edit has to remember to touch twice.\n\n**Worth considering**\n\n- None.\n\nEverything else checks out: the frontend-only design decision is sound and well-justified, all six acceptance criteria are otherwise met (immediate hide, exact-state restore since nothing is mutated, 5s auto-delete, done-state preserved, independent multi-undo via array+Map, 404 swallowed on the *timer* path), `TaskList.jsx`/`api.js`/backend correctly left untouched, and the CSS/a11y choices match the design doc and existing `.error`/`TaskCounts` conventions.\n\nVERDICT: changes-requested", "meta": {"native_type": "result", "subtype": "success", "session_id": "56a4d996-1bdf-4be3-85b0-80157f9d2990", "is_error": false, "total_cost_usd": 0.7536264}}
